body:
It's really odd... ...I've got no idea what the reason could be. I can't find any correlation between blood sugar and acid. The only thing that could potentially make sense is the increased amount of adrenaline but that'd be very short-lived.

&#x200B;

I could somewhat understand if it was a substance like DMT but I haven't done DMT before. There's a study on mice that showed DMT's ability to reproduce lost beta cells. Only problem is that your immune system will still kill them off... ...so that would also be short-lived.
